From 0dd7ae0ce28ac531913ec71284663d0eb9e19537 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:26:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple: charge J71t from computers and USB-C
 chargers at 2.4 A
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Charger source detection for the J71t Lightning port, as validated on
an iPad 5 Wi-Fi (S8003) on 2026-10-27:

- The Tristar power role reads the USB-C CC advertisement through
  Apple's USB-C to Lightning cable (3 A sources are capped at the
  2.4 A board maximum), keeps BC1.2 results across the cable's ID
  exchange, monitors idle Lightning lanes, and prefers an enumerated
  USB host over an early BC1.2 reading, so computers get the board
  maximum too.
- The D2365 charger restores the policy input limit after the PMIC's
  attach default (0x02) instead of treating it as a weak source.
- bq27xxx reports Discharging when the J71t gauge measures negative
  current, also at 100 %.
- The gadget core tells current-budget listeners why it notified
  them (no hardware operation).
- The diagnostics added to the lightning_state and charge7_state
  files are documented in sysfs-apple-charge{8,9,10}.

Computers (USB-A, and a Mac USB-C port through the USB-C to Lightning
cable), a USB-C wall charger and a Mac USB-C power adapter charge at
2.4 A, and the battery no longer drains on wall chargers. Charging is
5 V only; the iPad 5 has no USB Power Delivery.

From the validated charging update of the iPad 5 port
(https://github.com/brkosebay/omarchy-ipad5), filtered for OrchardLinux.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
