index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8f2b0b5f3bad871b105110b89ba5c7d2163b0a05
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-apple-charge10
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/*-001a/lightning_state
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
+Description:
+		source_epoch adds computer_seen: a positive USB data session
+		(connected, configured, or host-granted gadget evidence) observed
+		in this source epoch. It persists across USB suspend/reset and is
+		cleared by the same VBUS/ID/phase boundaries as other source policy.
+		A real computer supersedes prior divider/BC1.2/CC source results:
+		usb_type becomes SDP, with the charger's generic board ceiling.
+		bc_ua/bc_type remain diagnostic evidence and cannot cap that host.
+
+		bc_primary_mv and bc_secondary_mv report the most recent BC pin
+		measurements, distinct from passive dp_mv/dm_mv. Negative values
+		are errno/unavailable. They are reset on a new source epoch and
+		retained during a CC-only refresh. For ordinary USB, secondary D+
+		below 326 mV means CDP, at/above 326 mV means DCP. These are pin
+		voltages, not VBUS. A never-enumerating source keeps its proven
+		BC1.2/CC allowance, bounded by the existing charger policy.
diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-apple-charge8 b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-apple-charge8
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4577e4472878077678099953d64d12ac9b6382d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-apple-charge8
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/*-001a/lightning_state
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
+Description:
+		The charger_detect line adds cached diagnostics to the existing
+		Lightning snapshot. Reading it never starts a pin conversion.
+		stage/pin identify the last detection operation; error is its errno,
+		monitor_error is the role-monitor callback result (including a
+		refused callback), attempts/failures count this physical source,
+		retry_ms is the failure backoff (1000..60000 ms), poisoned means
+		ADC completion was uncertain and further triggers are prohibited
+		until reboot. Detach does not clear that poison; poison_stage and
+		poison_attach retain the operation and source epoch that latched it.
+
+		route is the last pre-monitor DX_CONTROL byte, adc_status the last
+		0x156 read. Negative values indicate errno or unavailable (-ENODATA).
+		dp_mv/dm_mv are passive divider samples, cc_mv the last opposite-pair
+		D+ sample for verified DigitalID 10 09 08 00 00 00. These are pin
+		voltages, never VBUS. sampled means classification completed.
+		Type C budgets come from stable CC advertisement (1500/3000 mA),
+		3 A requires BC1.2 charging-port evidence; otherwise it is capped
+		at 1500 mA. All budgets are bounded by the charger's board ceiling and supported current ladder.
+		Classification does not negotiate USB Power Delivery or change VBUS.
diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-apple-charge9 b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-apple-charge9
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d004764f00a493eee99f7be82e74c5ce52c80b5e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-apple-charge9
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+What:		/sys/class/power_supply/charger/charge7_state
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
+Description:
+		The attach_resets field counts successfully repaired D2365 0xa03
+		attach-default resets (0x02) in the first fifteen seconds of ownership
+		or a new source epoch. These do not create adaptive backoffs. A
+		policy step always uses its calibrated register code, including the
+		floor after other unexplained PMIC input reductions. Transport and
+		battery safety failures can defer a repair; live_ua remains readback,
+		not an assertion that nominal and actual currents are identical.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/*-001a/lightning_state
+Date:		October 2026
+Contact:	Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
+Description:
+		source_epoch records id, reason (boot, vbus-detach, digital-id or
+		accessory-phase), retained bc_ua/bc_type, cc_first_mv, lifetime
+		usb_events/usb_idle_events, data-session usb_generation and last
+		usb_event_source. Origin codes: 1 source forget, 2 base budget,
+		3 grant revoke, 4 suspend, 5 SETUP, 6 grant, 7 gadget state.
+		Idle notifications do not invalidate conversions; actual USB session
+		activity still does. A first ID refines the current epoch, preserving
+		verified BC evidence and scheduling one settled reclassification.
+		Changed IDs and phase drops to device/empty revoke the source even
+		when polling missed the VBUS-low interval. No poll-based guarantee
+		exists for an otherwise unobserved same-ID swap.
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
index a7ea39fdedaa0a313f2d77d138266502ff22720b..18bdc6547d8d97da217174ec6371cfca4f16a532 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_j71t_charger.c
